source java/net/sf/l2j/gameserver/model/actor/Summon.java 335-349 onSpawn
provenance hand
note The re-fire scan runs at the end of teleportTo, at the end of instantTeleportTo and when a summon spawns. It walks the NPCs of the regions around the creature's current region and does nothing while the creature has no region.
note teleportTo takes the creature out of its region and gives it back before the scan (onTeleported) only for a non-player or a player whose client is detached. Any other player (client attached, or no client) gets its region back later from the Appearing packet, which does not scan, so its teleportTo makes no call. instantTeleportTo keeps the creature's region (the pre-teleport one; it refreshes the known list from it) and scans the NPCs around that region, measuring distance from the new position. A summon's spawn scans from its spawn region.
note When the scan runs: if the creature is a playable, every scanned NPC within that NPC's see range (3D, strict, centre to centre) and at most 500 Z apart calls see-creature on it once. It is skipped when the acting player is spawn-protected or flying. There is no invisibility, silent-move or seen-set check, and the NPC's seen set is not updated.
note protected is the spawn-protection state of the acting player when the scan runs, not before the teleport. A player's onTeleported turns spawn protection on first when PlayerSpawnProtection > 0 (default 0), then teleports its summon to it. So under that config a detached player's teleportTo, and the teleportTo of a summon following its owner (from the owner's onTeleported, whether the owner's client is attached, through Appearing, or detached), scan with protected=true and make no call. instantTeleportTo and a summon's spawn do not run onTeleported, so the config does not change them.
note entry is teleportTo, instantTeleportTo or summon-spawn; client is the player's client state (attached, detached or none), - for other creatures; protection_config is whether PlayerSpawnProtection > 0.
row teleport-player-attached entry=teleportTo creature=player client=attached protection_config=off protected=false flying=false invisible=false in_range=true dz=0 calls=0
